  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Glass Shatter\n\nA glass shatter transition: a cracked-glass shader spreads from the centre of the first page, then 200 Voronoi shards break loose, fall with gravity and bounce while the second page is revealed behind them. WebGL over two built-in pages.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 12 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A dramatic cut where the screen breaks like glass and falls away to reveal the next scene.\n- Launch and announcement videos that need an impact moment.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need to shatter your own scenes: the block plays between its two built-in pages; copy the shader and shard code and feed it your own frames.\n- A quiet or corporate cut.\n\nVariables:\n- badge_a (string): Panel A badge, default \"Version 2 is almost here\"\n- headline_a (string): Panel A headline, default \"Everything you loved.|Now 10x faster.\"\n- charts (string): Panel A chart labels, default \"Render speed, Throughput, Reliability\"\n- features (string): Panel A features, default \"Instant deploys | Zero-downtime rollouts in under 3 seconds globally.; Encrypted end to end | AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit.; Real-time analytics | Sub-second queries across billions of events.\"\n- cta_a (string): Panel A button, default \"Get started\"\n- badge_b (string): Panel B badge, default \"Live now\"\n- headline_b (string): Panel B headline, default \"Version 2 is here\"\n- metrics (string): Panel B metrics, default \"10x | Render speed; 50% | File size; 99.99% | Reliability\"\n- cta_b (string): Panel B button, default \"See what is new\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Glass Shatter\n\n  A glass shatter transition: a cracked-glass shader spreads from the centre of the first page, then 200 Voronoi shards break loose, fall with gravity and bounce while the second page is revealed behind them. WebGL over two built-in pages.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/bd6cff8157a1a0ed5075527e673cc4f321fe9123/registry/blocks/vfx-shatter/vfx-shatter.html\n\n  Copyright HeyGen, Inc. and the Hyperframes contributors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version\n  2.0 (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain\n  a copy of the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable\n  law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n  BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for\n  the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n\n  Changes by usemosio/blocks: fills the host frame; rewritten from three.js (not loaded) to raw WebGL2 (the crack shader is unchanged apart from GLSL ES 3.0 syntax and the shard meshes are drawn with the same seeded Voronoi cells, fixed-step physics replayed from zero each frame, and Euler XYZ transforms); the two pages are drawn on 2D canvases from variables instead of being captured from live DOM with the experimental HTML-in-Canvas API, and their product copy is replaced by placeholders; the canvas is drawn at the `resolution` variable.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"vfx-shatter\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"12\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"badge_a\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A badge\", \"default\": \"Version 2 is almost here\"},\n    {\"id\": \"headline_a\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A headline\", \"description\": \"Use | for a line break; the last line takes the accent colour.\", \"default\": \"Everything you loved.|Now 10x faster.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"charts\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A chart labels\", \"description\": \"Three labels separated by commas.\", \"default\": \"Render speed, Throughput, Reliability\"},\n    {\"id\": \"features\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A features\", \"description\": \"Up to 3 features as \\\"Title | description\\\", separated by semicolons.\", \"default\": \"Instant deploys | Zero-downtime rollouts in under 3 seconds globally.; Encrypted end to end | AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit.; Real-time analytics | Sub-second queries across billions of events.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cta_a\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A button\", \"default\": \"Get started\"},\n    {\"id\": \"badge_b\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B badge\", \"default\": \"Live now\"},\n    {\"id\": \"headline_b\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B headline\", \"default\": \"Version 2 is here\"},\n    {\"id\": \"metrics\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B metrics\", \"description\": \"Three metrics as \\\"Value | label\\\", separated by semicolons.\", \"default\": \"10x | Render speed; 50% | File size; 99.99% | Reliability\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cta_b\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B button\", \"default\": \"See what is new\"},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the scene is drawn at, then scaled up. Page text needs 0.75.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Glass Shatter</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .vsh-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .vsh-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"vfx-shatter\" data-duration=\"12\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"vsh-clip\" class=\"vsh-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"12\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"vsh-canvas\" class=\"vsh-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"vfx-shatter\";\n            var DUR = 12;\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"vsh-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#000000\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"badge_a\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A badge\", \"default\": \"Version 2 is almost here\"}, {\"id\": \"headline_a\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A headline\", \"description\": \"Use | for a line break; the last line takes the accent colour.\", \"default\": \"Everything you loved.|Now 10x faster.\"}, {\"id\": \"charts\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A chart labels\", \"description\": \"Three labels separated by commas.\", \"default\": \"Render speed, Throughput, Reliability\"}, {\"id\": \"features\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A features\", \"description\": \"Up to 3 features as \\\"Title | description\\\", separated by semicolons.\", \"default\": \"Instant deploys | Zero-downtime rollouts in under 3 seconds globally.; Encrypted end to end | AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit.; Real-time analytics | Sub-second queries across billions of events.\"}, {\"id\": \"cta_a\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel A button\", \"default\": \"Get started\"}, {\"id\": \"badge_b\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B badge\", \"default\": \"Live now\"}, {\"id\": \"headline_b\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B headline\", \"default\": \"Version 2 is here\"}, {\"id\": \"metrics\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B metrics\", \"description\": \"Three metrics as \\\"Value | label\\\", separated by semicolons.\", \"default\": \"10x | Render speed; 50% | File size; 99.99% | Reliability\"}, {\"id\": \"cta_b\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Panel B button\", \"default\": \"See what is new\"}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the scene is drawn at, then scaled up. Page text needs 0.75.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * V.resolution));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * V.resolution));\n            root.style.background = \"#06080d\";\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var SANS = \"system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif\";\n            var U = W >= H ? Math.min(W / 1920, H / 1080) : W / 1080 * 1.2;\n            var DURATION = 12, SHARD_COUNT = 200, CRACK_START = 2.0, CRACK_END = 4.0, SHATTER_START = 4.0, SHATTER_SETTLE = 10.0;\n            function mulberry32(seed) {\n              return function () {\n                seed |= 0;\n                seed = (seed + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n                var t = Math.imul(seed ^ (seed >>> 15), 1 | seed);\n                t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            var rng = mulberry32(42);\n            function wrap(ctx, text, maxW) {\n              var words = String(text).split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean), lines = [], line = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var next = line ? line + \" \" + w : w;\n                if (line && ctx.measureText(next).width > maxW) { lines.push(line); line = w; } else line = next;\n              });\n              if (line) lines.push(line);\n              return lines;\n            }\n            function rrect(ctx, x, y, w, h, r) { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.roundRect(x, y, w, h, r); }\n            function pairs(s, n) { return String(s).split(\";\").map(function (c) { return c.split(\"|\").map(function (p) { return p.trim(); }); }).filter(function (c) { return c[0]; }).slice(0, n); }\n            function grad(ctx, x0, y0, x1, y1, c0, c1) { var g = ctx.createLinearGradient(x0, y0, x1, y1); g.addColorStop(0, c0); g.addColorStop(1, c1); return g; }\n            function pill(ctx, text, y, ink, fill, line) {\n              ctx.font = \"600 \" + 15 * U + \"px \" + SANS;\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width + 56 * U, h = 38 * U;\n              ctx.fillStyle = fill; rrect(ctx, (W - w) / 2, y, w, h, h / 2); ctx.fill();\n              ctx.strokeStyle = line; ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(1, U); rrect(ctx, (W - w) / 2, y, w, h, h / 2); ctx.stroke();\n              ctx.fillStyle = ink; ctx.textAlign = \"center\"; ctx.fillText(text, W / 2, y + h / 2 + 5 * U);\n              return h;\n            }\n            function button(ctx, text, y, c0, c1) {\n              ctx.font = \"700 \" + 18 * U + \"px \" + SANS;\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width + 80 * U, h = 52 * U;\n              ctx.fillStyle = grad(ctx, (W - w) / 2, y, (W + w) / 2, y + h, c0, c1);\n              rrect(ctx, (W - w) / 2, y, w, h, 12 * U); ctx.fill();\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#fff\"; ctx.textAlign = \"center\"; ctx.fillText(text, W / 2, y + h / 2 + 6 * U);\n            }\n            // Panel B first: it draws its confetti from the same seeded stream the shards use afterwards.\n            function drawPanelB(el) {\n              var ctx = el.getContext(\"2d\");\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = grad(ctx, 0, 0, W * 0.3, H, \"#0a0f1a\", \"#0f1628\"); ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              var dotColors = [\"#34d399\", \"#38bdf8\", \"#93c5fd\", \"#e5e5e5\", \"#fbbf24\"];\n              for (var d = 0; d < 60; d++) {\n                var sz = (4 + rng() * 12) * U, dx = rng() * W, dy = rng() * H;\n                ctx.fillStyle = dotColors[Math.floor(rng() * dotColors.length)];\n                ctx.globalAlpha = 0.06 + rng() * 0.12;\n                ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(dx + sz / 2, dy + sz / 2, sz / 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n              }\n              ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"alphabetic\";\n              var ms = pairs(V.metrics, 3), portrait = W < H;\n              var hs = 80 * U * (portrait ? 0.95 : 1), mw = (W * 0.86 - 2 * 24 * U) / 3, mh = 150 * U;\n              var total = 38 * U + 40 * U + hs + 48 * U + mh + 56 * U + 52 * U;\n              var y = (H - total) / 2;\n              ctx.font = \"600 \" + 15 * U + \"px \" + SANS;\n              pill(ctx, \"\\u2713 \" + V.badge_b, y, \"#34d399\", \"rgba(52,211,153,0.08)\", \"rgba(52,211,153,0.2)\");\n              y += 38 * U + 40 * U;\n              ctx.font = \"800 \" + hs + \"px \" + SANS; ctx.fillStyle = \"#f0f4f8\"; ctx.textAlign = \"center\";\n              var hw = ctx.measureText(V.headline_b).width; if (hw > W * 0.9) { hs *= W * 0.9 / hw; ctx.font = \"800 \" + hs + \"px \" + SANS; }\n              ctx.fillText(V.headline_b, W / 2, y + hs * 0.8);\n              y += hs + 48 * U;\n              var colors = [\"#34d399\", \"#38bdf8\", \"#93c5fd\"], x0 = (W - (mw * ms.length + 24 * U * (ms.length - 1))) / 2;\n              ms.forEach(function (m, i) {\n                var x = x0 + i * (mw + 24 * U);\n                ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.03)\"; rrect(ctx, x, y, mw, mh, 16 * U); ctx.fill();\n                ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.06)\"; ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(1, U); rrect(ctx, x, y, mw, mh, 16 * U); ctx.stroke();\n                ctx.font = \"800 \" + 52 * U * (portrait ? 0.8 : 1) + \"px \" + SANS; ctx.fillStyle = colors[i % 3]; ctx.textAlign = \"center\";\n                ctx.fillText(m[0], x + mw / 2, y + mh * 0.55);\n                ctx.font = \"500 \" + 15 * U + \"px \" + SANS; ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.4)\";\n                ctx.fillText(m[1] || \"\", x + mw / 2, y + mh * 0.8);\n              });\n              y += mh + 56 * U;\n              button(ctx, V.cta_b, y, \"#34d399\", \"#38bdf8\");\n            }\n            function drawPanelA(el) {\n              var ctx = el.getContext(\"2d\");\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = grad(ctx, 0, 0, W * 0.3, H, \"#0a0c14\", \"#111820\"); ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              var rg = ctx.createRadialGradient(W, 0, 0, W, 0, 600 * U); rg.addColorStop(0, \"rgba(56,189,248,0.06)\"); rg.addColorStop(1, \"rgba(56,189,248,0)\");\n              ctx.fillStyle = rg; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"alphabetic\";\n              var portrait = W < H, lines = String(V.headline_a).split(\"|\");\n              var hs = 88 * U * (portrait ? 0.9 : 1);\n              ctx.font = \"800 \" + hs + \"px \" + SANS;\n              var widest = Math.max.apply(null, lines.map(function (l) { return ctx.measureText(l.trim()).width; }));\n              if (widest > W * 0.9) hs *= W * 0.9 / widest;\n              var labels = String(V.charts).split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).slice(0, 3);\n              var feats = pairs(V.features, 3), colW = Math.min(W * 0.86, 1500 * U);\n              var chartH = 160 * U + 60 * U, featH = (portrait ? feats.length * 78 * U : 90 * U);\n              var total = 38 * U + 40 * U + lines.length * hs + 48 * U + chartH + 56 * U + featH + 56 * U + 52 * U;\n              var y = Math.max(20 * U, (H - total) / 2);\n              pill(ctx, V.badge_a, y, \"#38bdf8\", \"rgba(56,189,248,0.08)\", \"rgba(56,189,248,0.15)\");\n              y += 38 * U + 40 * U;\n              ctx.textAlign = \"center\";\n              lines.forEach(function (l, i) {\n                ctx.font = \"800 \" + hs + \"px \" + SANS;\n                ctx.fillStyle = i === lines.length - 1 && lines.length > 1 ? \"#38bdf8\" : \"#f0f4f8\";\n                ctx.fillText(l.trim(), W / 2, y + hs * 0.85); y += hs;\n              });\n              y += 48 * U;\n              var heights = [[60, 150], [90, 145], [110, 155]], gx = W / 2 - (3 * 150 * U + 2 * 40 * U) / 2;\n              labels.forEach(function (lb, i) {\n                var x = gx + i * (150 * U + 40 * U), base = y + 160 * U;\n                ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.08)\"; rrect(ctx, x, base - heights[i][0] * U, 64 * U, heights[i][0] * U, [6 * U, 6 * U, 0, 0]); ctx.fill();\n                ctx.fillStyle = grad(ctx, 0, base, 0, base - heights[i][1] * U, \"#38bdf8\", \"#2563eb\");\n                rrect(ctx, x + 72 * U, base - heights[i][1] * U, 64 * U, heights[i][1] * U, [6 * U, 6 * U, 0, 0]); ctx.fill();\n                ctx.font = \"500 \" + 14 * U + \"px \" + SANS; ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.4)\"; ctx.textAlign = \"center\";\n                ctx.fillText(lb, x + 68 * U, base + 28 * U);\n              });\n              y += chartH + 56 * U;\n              var fw = portrait ? colW : (colW - 2 * 32 * U) / Math.max(1, feats.length), fx = (W - (portrait ? colW : colW)) / 2;\n              feats.forEach(function (f, i) {\n                var x = portrait ? fx : fx + i * (fw + 32 * U), yy = portrait ? y + i * 78 * U : y;\n                ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(56,189,248,0.08)\"; rrect(ctx, x, yy, 44 * U, 44 * U, 10 * U); ctx.fill();\n                ctx.fillStyle = \"#38bdf8\"; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x + 22 * U, yy + 22 * U, 7 * U, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n                ctx.textAlign = \"left\"; ctx.font = \"600 \" + 16 * U + \"px \" + SANS; ctx.fillStyle = \"#e2e8f0\";\n                ctx.fillText(f[0], x + 58 * U, yy + 16 * U);\n                ctx.font = \"400 \" + 13 * U + \"px \" + SANS; ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\";\n                wrap(ctx, f[1] || \"\", fw - 70 * U).slice(0, 2).forEach(function (l, k) { ctx.fillText(l, x + 58 * U, yy + 38 * U + k * 19 * U); });\n              });\n              y += featH + 56 * U;\n              button(ctx, V.cta_a, y, \"#38bdf8\", \"#2563eb\");\n            }\n            var panels = [0, 1].map(function () { var c = document.createElement(\"canvas\"); c.width = cw; c.height = ch; return c; });\n            drawPanelB(panels[1]);\n            drawPanelA(panels[0]);\n            // Voronoi shard polygons: ~200 seeds (denser near the centre), each cell by intersecting bisectors.\n            var aspect = W / H, seeds = [], s, sx, sy;\n            for (s = 0; s < SHARD_COUNT; s++) {\n              if (s < SHARD_COUNT * 0.4) { var an = rng() * Math.PI * 2, rad = rng() * 0.35; sx = 0.5 * aspect + Math.cos(an) * rad * aspect; sy = 0.5 + Math.sin(an) * rad; }\n              else { sx = rng() * aspect; sy = rng(); }\n              seeds.push({ x: sx, y: sy });\n            }\n            function shardPolygons() {\n              var shards = [], ANGLES = 32, i, a, j, v;\n              for (i = 0; i < seeds.length; i++) {\n                var cx = seeds[i].x, cy = seeds[i].y, verts = [];\n                for (a = 0; a < ANGLES; a++) {\n                  var theta = (a / ANGLES) * Math.PI * 2, dx = Math.cos(theta), dy = Math.sin(theta), minT = 999;\n                  for (j = 0; j < seeds.length; j++) {\n                    if (j === i) continue;\n                    var mx = (cx + seeds[j].x) * 0.5, my = (cy + seeds[j].y) * 0.5, nx = seeds[j].x - cx, ny = seeds[j].y - cy;\n                    var denom = dx * nx + dy * ny;\n                    if (denom <= 0.0001) continue;\n                    var t = ((mx - cx) * nx + (my - cy) * ny) / denom;\n                    if (t > 0.001 && t < minT) minT = t;\n                  }\n                  if (dx > 0) { var tb = (aspect - cx) / dx; if (tb > 0 && tb < minT) minT = tb; }\n                  if (dx < 0) { var tb2 = -cx / dx; if (tb2 > 0 && tb2 < minT) minT = tb2; }\n                  if (dy > 0) { var tb3 = (1 - cy) / dy; if (tb3 > 0 && tb3 < minT) minT = tb3; }\n                  if (dy < 0) { var tb4 = -cy / dy; if (tb4 > 0 && tb4 < minT) minT = tb4; }\n                  if (minT < 998) verts.push({ x: cx + dx * minT, y: cy + dy * minT });\n                }\n                if (verts.length < 3) continue;\n                var centX = 0, centY = 0;\n                for (v = 0; v < verts.length; v++) { centX += verts[v].x; centY += verts[v].y; }\n                centX /= verts.length; centY /= verts.length;\n                verts.sort(function (p, q) { return Math.atan2(p.y - centY, p.x - centX) - Math.atan2(q.y - centY, q.x - centX); });\n                var tris = [];\n                for (v = 0; v < verts.length; v++) tris.push([{ x: centX, y: centY }, verts[v], verts[(v + 1) % verts.length]]);\n                shards.push({ centroidX: centX, centroidY: centY, triangles: tris });\n              }\n              return shards;\n            }\n            var shardData = shardPolygons();\n            // One vertex array per shard (mesh space, with the texture coordinate of panel A) and its seeded motion.\n            var shardGeo = [], phys = [];\n            shardData.forEach(function (sd) {\n              var pos = [];\n              sd.triangles.forEach(function (tri) { tri.forEach(function (p) { pos.push(p.x - aspect * 0.5, -(p.y - 0.5), p.x / aspect, p.y); }); });\n              if (pos.length < 12) return;\n              shardGeo.push(new Float32Array(pos));\n              var fx = sd.centroidX - aspect * 0.5, fy = sd.centroidY - 0.5, fl = Math.sqrt(fx * fx + fy * fy) + 0.001;\n              var ox = fx / fl, oy = fy / fl, speed = 0.3 + rng() * 0.7, upKick = 0.2 + rng() * 0.5;\n              phys.push({ cy: